It wastes game time, it wastes real time, and it's unneccessary.  I'd
rather save time and have my melee characters skip ranged combat
whenever they can safely do so.   I really don't care how much damage
ranged combat can do.  I can beat the entire game perfectly fine with
my primary combat method doing less than 20 damage per turn, so I
really don't care that ranged combat can easily go over 200 damage per
turn.  Again, I don't see a need to overkill monsters.

Also, for most of the Gnomish Mines levels, I argue that it's often
safer for melee characters to use primarily melee than ranged.  Many of
the Mines levels involve a giant open area, where all the monsters try
mobbing you at the same time, and you can't always see where a
chokepoint is.  If a melee character is wasting turns throwing one
projectile per turn, you are at a higher risk for multiple monsters
being in melee range at the same time.  However, if a melee character
runs up to the monsters, and kills them with melee, he can usually
avoid being mobbed by multiple monsters at the same time.  The most
excellent reason why you want to avoid being mobbed by 'h' monsters in
the mines is because some of them are wielding weapons, which can make
them an actual threat to your character.  If you are being attacked by
more than 1 monster at the same time, and 1 of them has a weapon, then
it is a total pain to figure out which monster you should hit first.
However, if you are meleeing them 1-at-a-time, then it becomes very
easy to figure out which ones are dangerous.



